\section{Side channels}{

AES runs on the CPU's AES instructions where it has them, and on a
table-based software fallback otherwise; \code{crypt_info()} reports which, in
\code{build_flags$aes_implementation}. On the fallback both AES and GHASH, the
authentication half of GCM, read tables at addresses that depend on the
key. See \link{crypt_aes_cbc_nopad} for what that exposes.
